var _ = declareRoute(routeDecl{
	Method:      http.MethodGet,
	Pattern:     "/api/v1/issues/{key}/tree",
	Auth:        authAny,
	Description: fmt.Sprintf("One issue's tree as the caller may see it, in the tree's own order, from the scope GET /api/v1/issues/{key} reads in: {issue, view, version, converted, tree, view_of, documents, nodes, document_nodes, tuples, cursor, remaining, comments_before}. With no ?view= it answers the skeleton of the issue's tree: every node but a document, a document version, the prose of a role document, a block of the issue's other documents - each but its spec, its Verification document, its plan and its tree's own fragment - and a comment off its comment page - the issue's own node, then each node before its children, under the issue its memo callout first, then under each node its asks, comments, messages, lenses and risks by when each was made, then its ranked children by rank, then the rest by when each was made, each tie by the lower id, then each node of the issue whose parent is a node of an issue above - and each child issue, each node of an issue under it placed under one of its nodes, each check of an issue under it whose serves names one of its requirements, under the first requirement it serves, with that check's results, and each such plan node, read-only and marked with their issue; then, marked as context, each lens_kind and constraint a has_kind or constrained_by of a node it holds names that the tree does not hold, one level out, each interaction a changed_by_run of such a node names, through the caller's visibility, and each decision's decided_by person or session. ?kind=, repeated, one kind each, filters that read to the nodes of the kinds it names, each with every ancestor up to the issue, an ancestor of another kind marked as context, in the walk's order, with the context the read with no view carries for the nodes it returns: a typed block's type (each typed block of the block schema: callout, ask, criterion, requirement, check, plan_task, decision, reading), comment, message, issue (a child issue), lens, risk, constraint, result, finding (a block naming its lens) or prose (a block that opens no typed block). callout takes the issue's memo alone, ask each ask's own node and never an ask block, comment each comment tied to no text with the replies under it and each comment on the text of a node the skeleton does not hold, as the read with no view answers it, and check each check of an issue under it under the requirement it serves, its results only beside kind=result; an item's own blocks stand with their item. kind=block, an empty kind, any other value, and kind beside view or v are 400 INVALID_QUERY naming kind and the values it takes. Every read, with a view, with kind or with neither, also carries each comment on the text of a node it returns, with every comment of its thread: a comment of a thread a person wrote in as a node of the tree, any other as context, and in a view each as context; a comment on the text of a node the skeleton holds comes only with that node. Beside its nodes the read with no view answers document_nodes, each document of kind doc GET /api/v1/issues/{key} lists, in that order, {artifact_id, slug, block_count}, block_count the number of blocks GET /api/v1/artifacts/{id}/blocks lists for it, where a page reads the blocks of a document its reader opens. Each read's comment page is the %[1]d newest of the comments it carries by made_at and then by id, each with the nodes under it; comments_before is <made_at>,<id>, the made_at (RFC 3339, in UTC, with microseconds) and the id of the page's oldest comment, where older comments remain, and null where none does. ?comments_before=<made_at>,<id>, beside the same view or kinds, answers the %[1]d comments that read carries older than that position, with the nodes under them and their tuples, and no other node, and its own comments_before; a comment whose parent the answer does not hold - the issue, an ask, a comment of another page - names that parent as its parent and stands under the issue, by made_at and then by id. A comments_before of another shape, one that no older comment of the issue follows, and one beside cursor are 400 INVALID_QUERY. ?view=spec, verification, plan or decisions answers that query's nodes, each role query, and its fixed context, each role context: on a child, the requirements of the issues above that its checks serve and its design blocks; on the verification view, every requirement node of the issue, served or not, so a requirement no check serves is in the answer, and each other requirement a check serves, and on a parent each check of an issue under it serving one of its requirements, with its results; on the plan view, every plan node of the whole tree and each issue as its two halves, each with its position, needs and size from the ordered read, in that one order. The decisions view answers each question the issue asked by its ask's own node, each decision, and each reading under a decision or under an answered question's node, keyed and shaped as GET /api/v1/issues/{key}/decisions answers them; a request for a document's approval is an ask too and no node of this query. The spec and the verification views also answer, as context, each decision and each answered ask whose shaped names one of their nodes and each constraint a constrained_by of one of them names, with those tuples; a view answers no document_nodes. ?v= with a view reads the query as of the store revision that version of its query node recorded; a version the query node does not have is 404 QUERY_VERSION_NOT_FOUND, as every version of the decisions query is until that query records one, one it has that holds no record of the revision it read - written before that record, deferred before its pass, or rendered off a mismatched tree - is 404 QUERY_VERSION_NOT_RECORDED naming the version, and v with no view is 400 INVALID_QUERY. Each node: kind and id as the store keys it, block_id, supertag, issue and read_only for a node of another issue, role, parent {kind, id, supertag, first_line, issue}, rank, placement_seq, author, state, visibility, made_at, edited_at on a comment or a message its author edited, deleted_at and deleted_by on one its author deleted, attributes, text and, for a caller that sent Dispatch-Trees: 1, text_tree, the tree its kind's own read answers; no_conversation where no conversation node stands above it; document {artifact_id, slug, position} on a typed block of a role document; ask {options, urgency, multiple, answer, selected, answered_by, answered_at} on an ask, its question its text, each answer member null where it holds none, as on a declined ask; decision, the Decisions read's members with uncertainty and uncertainty_reason, on a decision and an answered ask; result {verdict, retracted, check_version, check_sha256}; check {text_sha256, changed_version}; plan on the plan view; checks on a requirement, how many checks of the issue and of each issue under it serve it at the read's cut, as GET /api/v1/issues/{key}/coverage counts them; title on a session that stamped one, the newest it stamped; anchor {artifact_id, block_id, mark_id, version, quote, orphaned} on a comment whose anchor is a document's, as the comments read answers it; and converted, tree, view_of and documents on an issue. A node the caller may not see is left out, and each node under it stands under the nearest node above it the caller may see, after that node's own children. tuples is every relation between two nodes of the answer, each end named by its kind and id. One page holds at most %[2]d nodes and at most 2,000,000 bytes of JSON; a larger answer answers cursor, the next node, which ?cursor= reads from, and remaining, how many nodes the read holds after the page; each context node stands on the first page holding a node one of its tuples names, and one no such tuple names on the last.", issueTreeCommentPageSize, issueTreePageSize),
	Handler:     (*server).getIssueTree,
	Read:        readEntry{Writes: readWritesNothing, WriteNote: "Reads one issue's tree through the visibility predicate, as GET /api/v1/issues/{key} reads the issue, and lists the blocks of each role document the page holds through the document service (docs.Service.Blocks). " + docsCompactionNote + " Its display trees, with Dispatch-Trees: 1, are read as every read's are (readDisplayTrees)."},
	Shape:       routeShape{Status: http.StatusOK, Response: model.IssueTreeRead{}, Params: issueTreeQuery{}},
})
